      "message": "@tomhughes@chromium.org\nCan you please elaborate more regarding your comment:\n\nIn the quincy board, we enable [CONFIG_ARM_MPU](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/boards/google/quincy/google_quincy_defconfig;l\u003d25#:~:text\u003d24-,25,-26). `config ARM_MPU` selects [MPU](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/arch/common/Kconfig;l\u003d29?q\u003d%22config%20ARM_MPU%22\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d28-,29,-30) i.e. enables it. Are you suggesting that we add `depends on MPU`, which makes this option unavailable to configure if we do not have `CONFIG_MPU` enabled?\n\n```\nconfig NPCX_RAM_LOCK\n\tbool \"Enable NPCX RAM lock function\"\n\tdepends on MPU\n\tdefault n\n```\n\nby the way, I do not believe we need to specify `default n`. It is n by default for the bool type.",
