      "writtenOn": "2025-07-11T21:36:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does not compile when we make it depend on MPU. It seems it is creating a circular dependency. Based on the gemini analysis, this is how the circular dependency is created:\n\n```\nZTEST (the Zephyr testing framework)\nuparrow (selects)\nHW_TEST_RAM_LOCK\nuparrow (depends on)\nNPCX_RAM_LOCK\nuparrow (depends on)\nMPU\nuparrow (depends on a configuration related to CACHE like XTENSA_MPU which depends on !CACHE)\nCACHE\nuparrow (depends on CACHE_MANAGEMENT)\nCACHE_MANAGEMENT\nuparrow (selects/depends on various drivers, including some related to I2C, FDC2X1X)\nFDC2X1X\nuparrow (selects/depends on I2C)\nI2C\nuparrow (depends on/selects various other features, including REQUIRES_FULL_LIBC indirectly)\nREQUIRES_FULL_LIBC\nuparrow (depends on/selects various features, including HWINFO)\nHWINFO\nuparrow (implies/depends on SHELL)\nSHELL\nuparrow (selects)\nZTEST_SHELL (which then directly selects ZTEST)\n...and back to ZTEST again!\n```",
      "parentUuid": "bc932b81_da09de5a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 67,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "60b12a3999f965bf2b86282cdb5dcf665c683eab",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
